#he[אָב]; #emph[father];; the #emph[constr.]; #he[אֲבִי];, like #he[אֲחִי]; and #he[בְּנִי]; (which occurs once), belongs to the connective forms discussed in #xref(<p90k>)[§ 90#h(0.18em)#emph[k];];, which serve as the model for the #emph[Ḥireq compaginis];. However, #he[אַב]; also occurs in compound proper names, e.g. #he[אַבְשָׁלוֹם];, beside #he[אֲבִֽישָׁלוֹם];, etc.; also #bref("Gen 17:4f."); #he[אַב־הֲמוֹן]; for the purpose of explaining the name #he[אב\[ר\]הם];. On the plur. #he[אָבוֹת]; see #xref(<p87p>)[§ 87#h(0.18em)#emph[p];];.

#he[אָח]; #emph[brother];. The plur. #emph[absol.]; #he[אַחִים]; has #emph[Dageš forte implicitum]; (#xref(<p22c>)[§ 22#h(0.18em)#emph[c];];); #he[אֶחָיו]; stands for #he[אַחָיו]; according to the phonetic law stated in #xref(<p27q>)[§ 27#h(0.18em)#emph[q];];, and so also #he[אֶחָֽי]; in #emph[pause]; for #he[אַחָֽי];. The sharpening of the #he[ח]; merely serves to keep the preceding #emph[Pathaḥ]; short, as in #he[גְּמַלִּים];, etc. (#xref(<p93ee>)[§ 93#h(0.18em)#emph[ee];];).

#he[אֶחָד]; #emph[one]; (for #he[אַחָד];, likewise with #emph[Dageš forte implicitum];, #xref(<p22c>)[§ 22#h(0.18em)#emph[c];];, cf. #xref(<p27q>)[§ 27#h(0.18em)#emph[q];];), #emph[constr.]; and otherwise in close connection, #he[אַחַד];, #bref("Gen 48:22");, #bref("2 Sam 17:22");, #bref("Isa 27:12");, #origpage("283") <orig-283>;

